{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T11:47:29.512Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Fixtures**: Copied `fixture/files/` and `fixture-rows/` byte-for-byte (verified with `diff -r`, `.run/` folders included) into `crates/kernel/storage/tests/fixtures/`.\n\n**Reading code** (all under `src/read/`):\n- `sections.rs` — `ResultSections` + `parse_result_sections`, hand-written to mirror TypeScript's `parseResultSections` (heading case/spacing/colon drift, unknown heading ends the section, repeated headings append, inline `touched:`, CRLF, and the `None`/list-marker absence rule), no regex crate.\n- `results.rs` — `TaskDisclosure` and the `.run/results/<n>.md` reader (digits+`.md` only, numeric order, files with a real disclosure only).\n- `manual.rs` — `ManualEdit` + `read_manual_edits` using `yaml-rust2` for frontmatter and `markdown_body`, ordered by `kept_at` then file name.\n- `text.rs` gained `frontmatter_yaml`; `snapshot.rs` gained the `disclosures` field filled by `read_change`; `read/mod.rs` and `lib.rs` re-export the five public items.\n\n**Tests**: `reading_files.rs` (the five scenarios, one case per table row), plus `reading_files_sections.rs` and `reading_files_records.rs` for the edges.\n\n**Verification**: `cargo test -p osq-kernel-storage --test reading_files` passes; `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` exits 0 (fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, all workspace tests, corpus included). I also ran cargo-mutants over every changed source file: the single missed mutant (`||` in `result_number`, an equivalent branch) was removed, and all mutants are now caught.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/212-rust-storage-file-tables/.run/results/1.md`."}}
